From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: a file's settings keep the subtitle position

Text subtitles of an episode started with Play Next, while the one before
was ending, sat at the top of the screen for the whole episode. Stopping and
playing again put them back at the bottom.

The renderer works the position out itself, and only again when the frame
height changes. Play Next keeps the player and its renderer: the position
is worked out from the first frame, and then playback start loads the new
file's video settings and hands them to the player. A file stores no
subtitle position, so they carry 0, which the renderer takes as its
position - the top - and the frame height has not changed for it to work
it out again. A fresh start loads the settings before the renderer has a
frame, so it works the position out after them.

A file's settings now keep the subtitle position the player already has.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -7722,6 +7722,11 @@
 
 void CVideoPlayer::SetVideoSettings(CVideoSettings& settings)
 {
+  // a file stores no subtitle position: keep the one the renderer set for this resolution
+  const CVideoSettings current{m_processInfo->GetVideoSettings()};
+  settings.m_subtitleVerticalPosition = current.m_subtitleVerticalPosition;
+  settings.m_subtitleVerticalPositionSave = current.m_subtitleVerticalPositionSave;
+
   m_processInfo->SetVideoSettings(settings);
   m_renderManager.SetVideoSettings(settings);
   m_renderManager.SetDelay(static_cast<int>(settings.m_AudioDelay * 1000.0f));
